# Node record

The atlas graph and the formal statements its problems get. Node ids are built
here, once, so every source places its problems in the same tree:
`cohort:<c>`, `collection:<c>/<k>`, `category:<c>/<k>/<g>` and `problem:<id>`.
The vocabularies match the coordinator's schema
(`database/migrations/0004_factory.sql`), which enforces them.

## Note
One node: `parentId` is `none` at a root, `problemId` names the problem of a
problem, statement or lemma node, `stage` is where it stands and `rank` its
scheduling priority in basis points.

## A Node has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a parentId, which is Option of Text.
    a problemId, which is Option of Text.
    a kind, which is Text.
    a label, which is Text.
    a stage, which is Text.
    a rank, which is Int.

## Note
A formal statement: a kernel-vernacular document defining `goalName` as a `Prop`.
A proof is accepted only as a theorem of exactly that type, checked after this
document byte for byte; `sha256` is what a result is bound to. `route` is `A`
(translated from Lean), `B` (an informal problem given a Lean statement first) or
`C` (written directly in the vernacular).

## A Statement has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a problemId, which is Text.
    a document, which is Text.
    a sha256, which is Text.
    a goalName, which is Text.
    a route, which is Text.
    a reviewState, which is Text.
    an author, which is Text.
    a model, which is Text.
    a createdAt, which is Int.

## Note
The node kinds, stages and review states the schema allows.

## To nodeKinds () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["root", "cohort", "collection", "category", "problem", "statement", "lemma"].

## Note
A node's stage: ranked, being formalized, formalized, worked on, then settled.

## To nodeStages () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["ranked", "formalizing", "formalized", "in_progress", "partial", "solved", "refuted", "invalid_formalization"].

## Note
A statement's review: written, under review, accepted (one per problem), rejected, replaced.

## To reviewStates () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["draft", "reviewing", "accepted", "rejected", "superseded"].

## Note
The ids of the graph's levels: a cohort, a collection in it, a category in that,
and a problem.

## To cohortNodeId (cohort: Text) -> Text:
    Return "cohort:" + cohort.

## To collectionNodeId (cohort: Text, collection: Text) -> Text:
    Return "collection:" + cohort + "/" + collection.

## To categoryNodeId (cohort: Text, collection: Text, category: Text) -> Text:
    Return "category:" + cohort + "/" + collection + "/" + category.

## To problemNodeId (problemId: Text) -> Text:
    Return "problem:" + problemId.

## Note
A node that has just been ranked.

## To rankedNode (id: Text, parent: Option of Text, problem: Option of Text, kind: Text, label: Text, rank: Int) -> Node:
    Return a new Node with id id and parentId parent and problemId problem and kind kind and label label and stage "ranked" and rank rank.

## Test: a node and a statement round-trip through their derived codecs

Let n be rankedNode(categoryNodeId("U", "green", "comb"), some collectionNodeId("U", "green"), none, "category", "Combinatorics", 4200).
Expect that fromJson_Node(toJson_Node(n)) is equal to a new Ok with value n.
Let mutable s be a new Statement with id "stmt:ab" and problemId "opdp:116" and document "Definition goal : Prop := True." and sha256 "ab".
Set s's goalName to "goal".
Set s's route to "C".
Set s's reviewState to "draft".
Set s's author to "c1".
Set s's model to "m".
Set s's createdAt to 5.
Expect that fromJson_Statement(toJson_Statement(s)) is equal to a new Ok with value s.

## Test: node ids name their level and place

Expect that cohortNodeId("UnsolvedMath") is equal to "cohort:UnsolvedMath".
Expect that categoryNodeId("U", "green", "comb") is equal to "category:U/green/comb".
Expect that problemNodeId("opdp:116") is equal to "problem:opdp:116".
Expect that (rankedNode("x", none, none, "cohort", "X", 7))'s stage is equal to "ranked".

## Test: the graph's vocabularies are the schema's

Expect that length of nodeKinds() is equal to 7.
Expect that nodeStages() contains "invalid_formalization".
Expect that reviewStates() contains "accepted".

## Test: a ranked node keeps its kind whether or not it belongs to a problem

For all booleans owned:
    Let mutable problem: Option of Text be none.
    If owned:
        Set problem to some "opdp:1".
    Expect that (rankedNode("n", none, problem, "problem", "P", 1))'s kind is equal to "problem".
